                      (    forth6809.asm):03857                                   ; discards the frame automatically and
                      (    forth6809.asm):03858                                   ; correctly on every path - traced and
                      (    forth6809.asm):03859                                   ; confirmed: with no enclosing DO (compiled
                      (    forth6809.asm):03860                                   ; count 0), with one enclosing DO and no
                      (    forth6809.asm):03861                                   ; prior UNLOOP (discards the full 8-byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):03862                                   ; frame correctly). The one combination that
                      (    forth6809.asm):03863                                   ; broke was UNLOOP immediately before EXIT -
                      (    forth6809.asm):03864                                   ; UNLOOP discarding 6 of the 8 bytes itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):03865                                   ; then EXITUNLOOP unconditionally discarding
                      (    forth6809.asm):03866                                   ; a full 8 more, overshooting into whatever
                      (    forth6809.asm):03867                                   ; sat below (typically the caller's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):03868                                   ; return address) and branching into random
                      (    forth6809.asm):03869                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):03870                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):03871                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):03872                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):03873                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):03874                                   ; a second, conflicting discard mechanism.
