F318 4D               (    forth6809.asm):05000                  TSTA          ; BUG FIX: was a bare "BPL SDPOS" right after
                      (    forth6809.asm):05001                                  ; PULU - PULU doesn't affect condition codes
                      (    forth6809.asm):05002                                  ; on genuine 6809 (same class as TRYNUM's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):05003                                  ; PULU-then-compare fix elsewhere in this
                      (    forth6809.asm):05004                                  ; file), so BPL was testing whatever flags an
                      (    forth6809.asm):05005                                  ; unrelated, earlier instruction happened to
                      (    forth6809.asm):05006                                  ; leave set, not the sign of the value just
                      (    forth6809.asm):05007                                  ; popped. TSTA explicitly tests D's high byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):05008                                  ; (bit 7 of A reflects the full 16-bit value's
                      (    forth6809.asm):05009                                  ; sign) immediately before the branch that
                      (    forth6809.asm):05010                                  ; depends on it. Confirmed via MAME debugger:
                      (    forth6809.asm):05011                                  ; "-123 S>D" returned high cell 0 instead of
                      (    forth6809.asm):05012                                  ; -1 - no sign extension was happening at all.
